OpenAICompatible::transcription_response (lib/Langertha/Role/OpenAICompatible.pm:506-510) runs parse_response (json->decode) and returns ->{text}. OpenAI/Groq/faster-whisper accept response_format=text|srt|vtt (plain-text bodies) — passable via %extra, and the POD advertises %extra pass-through.

Repro (offline): $whisper->transcription_response(HTTP::Response->new(200,"OK",["Content-Type"=>"text/plain"],"hello world\n")) -> croak "malformed JSON string ... at Role/HTTP.pm line 141" (no engine name, no hint).
Also: response_format=verbose_json returns segments/words/duration/language but only ->{text} survives (callers asking for timestamps lose them silently).

Fix: branch on the response Content-Type (application/json -> decode; text/* -> return decoded_content); for verbose_json consider returning the text and keeping the full payload reachable (the chat Response pattern), or document that transcription_response returns text only and callers wanting segments must parse the raw response. Add response-parsing tests with captures.
